# Cursor commit-message generation (sparkle)

Fleet guidance for Cursor Source Control "Generate commit message". Newer `.cursor/rules` / `AGENTS.md` are not applied
to that button today — this legacy file is. Keep in sync with `commitlint.config.cjs` and `docs/quality.md`.

When generating a Git commit message for this repository:

- Use Conventional Commits only: `type(optional-scope): subject`
- Allowed types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert, deps
- Choose `type` from the **diff contents**, not from OpenSpec change names or folder titles
- `feat` / `fix` only when the commit changes shipped behaviour (workflows, scripts, runtime configs, product code)
- OpenSpec archive / opsx cleanup alone (e.g. `/opsx-archive`: move under `openspec/changes/archive/`, sync deltas into
  `openspec/specs/`) → `chore` (optional scope `openspec`), **never** `feat` — that would falsely minor-bump Release
  `version_bump: auto`
- Docs-only → `docs`; CI workflow wiring → `ci`; Renovate-style dependency bumps → `deps`
- Breaking changes: `feat!:` / `fix!:` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Subject: imperative mood, ~72 chars, no trailing period
- Do not write a multi-paragraph changelog; one subject line is enough unless a short body is needed for breaking
  changes
